{
  "info": {
    "name": "Peppa Conditional Settlements",
    "description": "Partner-facing API for holding payments on a seller's Stripe account and releasing them when a condition is met.\n\n**Set up**\n1. Import the environment file alongside this collection.\n2. Set `base_url` (e.g. http://localhost:8000) and `api_key` from the merchant dashboard → API Keys.\n3. Work through the folders in order. Requests save ids into variables as you go, so the later ones need no editing.\n\n**Order matters.** Create a seller before holding a payment, and set a rule before expecting a release.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{api_key}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "connected_account_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "connected_account_row_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "hold_reference",
      "value": "ORDER-1001"
    },
    {
      "key": "rule_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "supplier_account_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "freight_account_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "split_reference",
      "value": "SHIPMENT-1001"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 · Sellers",
      "description": "Onboard a seller and check they are ready to be paid.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create seller account",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('created', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.account) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('connected_account_id', body.data.account.account_id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('connected_account_row_id', body.data.account.id);",
                  "  console.log('Onboarding URL:', body.data.onboarding_url);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/connected-accounts",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "connected-accounts"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"seller_email\": \"seller+{{$timestamp}}@example.com\",\n  \"country\": \"GB\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Creates the seller's Stripe account, sets it to manual payouts, and returns a link for them to finish Stripe's onboarding.\n\nThe link expires in about five minutes. Open the `onboarding_url` from the response (it is also logged to the Postman console) and complete it before testing holds — `can_hold_funds` stays false until Stripe approves the seller.\n\nCountries supported today: GB, US."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List sellers",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/connected-accounts",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "connected-accounts"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get one seller",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/connected-accounts/{{connected_account_row_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "connected-accounts",
                "{{connected_account_row_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "`can_hold_funds` is the only field you need before charging. When it is false, `hold_blockers` explains why in plain words."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Fresh onboarding link",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/connected-accounts/{{connected_account_row_id}}/onboarding-link",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "connected-accounts",
                "{{connected_account_row_id}}",
                "onboarding-link"
              ]
            },
            "description": "For a seller who abandoned the flow or let the link lapse. Stripe's links are short-lived, so generate one per visit rather than storing it."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Re-sync from Stripe",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/connected-accounts/{{connected_account_row_id}}/sync",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "connected-accounts",
                "{{connected_account_row_id}}",
                "sync"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Normally unnecessary — the Stripe webhook keeps this current. Useful when testing locally without webhooks reaching you."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Seller dashboard",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/connected-accounts/{{connected_account_row_id}}/dashboard",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "connected-accounts",
                "{{connected_account_row_id}}",
                "dashboard"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Everything a seller can see about their own money: balance, payouts, every hold with a plain-English explanation, and their onboarding state.\n\nSellers have no Stripe dashboard, so this is the only place they can look. Render it in your own product.\n\nIf Stripe is unreachable, `balance.source` is `unavailable` and `balance.available` is **null**, not zero."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Embedded component session",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/connected-accounts/{{connected_account_row_id}}/account-session",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "connected-accounts",
                "{{connected_account_row_id}}",
                "account-session"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"components\": [\"payouts\", \"account_management\"]\n}"
            },
            "description": "A short-lived secret for Stripe's embedded components, so a seller can manage bank details and identity. Peppa is barred from touching those itself."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 · Release rules",
      "description": "What releases a held payment. Set at least one before expecting anything to release.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create rule — buyer confirmation",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (b.data) pm.collectionVariables.set('rule_id', b.data.id);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/settlement-rules",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "settlement-rules"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Buyer confirmed receipt\",\n  \"condition_type\": \"buyer_confirmation\",\n  \"release_percentage\": 100,\n  \"priority\": 100\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create rule — 7 day timer",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/settlement-rules",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "settlement-rules"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Release after 7 days\",\n  \"condition_type\": \"elapsed_days\",\n  \"days\": 7,\n  \"priority\": 200\n}"
            },
            "description": "Fires from the hourly sweep (`php artisan settlements:process-holds`), not from an endpoint.\n\nAlways have a timer. Without one, a payment where nobody confirms and nobody approves sits until Stripe's deadline forces it out."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create rule — manual approval, 50%",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/settlement-rules",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "settlement-rules"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Half on approval\",\n  \"condition_type\": \"manual_approval\",\n  \"release_percentage\": 50,\n  \"priority\": 300\n}"
            },
            "description": "Partial releases are capped at what remains, so two 60% rules pay out 100%, not 120%."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create rule — rejected, timer too long",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('rejected with 422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/settlement-rules",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "settlement-rules"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Too long\",\n  \"condition_type\": \"elapsed_days\",\n  \"days\": 120\n}"
            },
            "description": "Expected to fail. Stripe would force-release before a 120 day rule could fire, so the rule is refused rather than silently never firing."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List rules",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/settlement-rules",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "settlement-rules"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update rule",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/settlement-rules/{{rule_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "settlement-rules",
                "{{rule_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Buyer confirmed receipt (renamed)\",\n  \"is_active\": true\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Deactivate rule",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/settlement-rules/{{rule_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "settlement-rules",
                "{{rule_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Deactivates rather than deletes, so holds it released keep the explanation of why they released."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3 · Holds",
      "description": "A payment waiting on a condition. Needs a seller whose `can_hold_funds` is true.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Open a hold",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('held', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (b.data) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('hold_reference', b.data.reference);",
                  "  console.log('Release by:', b.data.release_by);",
                  "}",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 409) {",
                  "  console.log('Seller not ready:', JSON.stringify(b.blockers));",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"reference\": \"ORDER-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"connected_account_id\": \"{{connected_account_id}}\",\n  \"amount\": 100.00,\n  \"currency\": \"GBP\",\n  \"payment_intent_id\": \"pi_test_placeholder\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "`reference` is yours — use your own order number. You never store an id of Peppa's.\n\nIdempotent: the same reference twice returns the existing hold with 200 rather than opening a second one.\n\nReturns **409** with a `blockers` array if the seller is not ready. That is the expected response until the seller finishes Stripe onboarding."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List holds",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds?per_page=25",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "per_page",
                  "value": "25"
                },
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "held",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "expiring",
                  "value": "1",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Within 7 days of the Stripe deadline"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get a hold with its event trail",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/{{hold_reference}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "{{hold_reference}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The `events` array is the record of why money moved: every state change, who caused it, and when."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4 · Releasing",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Buyer confirms",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/{{hold_reference}}/confirm",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "{{hold_reference}}",
                "confirm"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Evaluates the merchant's `buyer_confirmation` rules. If none is active, nothing releases and the attempt is recorded in the event trail — so a missing rule is visible rather than silent."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Manual approval",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/{{hold_reference}}/approve",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "{{hold_reference}}",
                "approve"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"actor\": \"ops:jane\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "`actor` is a label you assert. It is recorded on the audit trail, not used for authorisation."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refund (partial)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/{{hold_reference}}/refund",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "{{hold_reference}}",
                "refund"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"amount\": 30.00,\n  \"reason\": \"One item missing\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Omit `amount` to refund everything remaining. Refunds come out of the seller's balance, which is where the money is."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5 · Disputes",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Raise a dispute",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/{{hold_reference}}/dispute",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "{{hold_reference}}",
                "dispute"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"reason\": \"Item never arrived\",\n  \"actor\": \"buyer\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Freezes the hold completely. No rule fires, timers are ignored, and the hourly sweep leaves it alone.\n\n**A dispute does not pause Stripe's holding deadline.** The money still has to leave the seller's account by the same date."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Confirm while disputed — no release",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('still disputed', () => pm.expect(b.data.status).to.eql('disputed'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/{{hold_reference}}/confirm",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "{{hold_reference}}",
                "confirm"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Run this after raising a dispute. It returns 200 but the hold stays `disputed` and nothing is paid out — a timer must never release money that is being argued over."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Resolve — pay the seller",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/{{hold_reference}}/dispute/resolve",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "{{hold_reference}}",
                "dispute",
                "resolve"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"outcome\": \"release\",\n  \"actor\": \"ops:jane\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "`outcome` is one of `release`, `refund` or `resume`. Returns 409 if the hold is not disputed."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Resolve — refund the buyer",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/{{hold_reference}}/dispute/resolve",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "{{hold_reference}}",
                "dispute",
                "resolve"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"outcome\": \"refund\",\n  \"actor\": \"ops:jane\"\n}"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6 · Error cases",
      "description": "Worth running once so the failure shapes are familiar.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "No API key → 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Unknown reference → 404",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/NO-SUCH-ORDER",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "NO-SUCH-ORDER"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Dispute with no reason → 422",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/{{hold_reference}}/dispute",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "{{hold_reference}}",
                "dispute"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Resolve a hold that is not disputed → 409",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/holds/{{hold_reference}}/dispute/resolve",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "holds",
                "{{hold_reference}}",
                "dispute",
                "resolve"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"outcome\": \"release\",\n  \"actor\": \"ops:jane\"\n}"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "7 · Split payments",
      "description": "One payment divided between several participants the moment it is paid. Each share goes straight into its participant's own account and is held there until a rule releases it; Peppa never holds the money. Create two participants and finish their onboarding, create the rule, open the hold, pay it through payment_url, then report the milestone.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create participant — supplier",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
